.TH "RAPTOR-EXTRACT" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-extract \- Build a standalone model from one hierarchy (its In node becomes Start, its Out node End) and save it, or list what crosses its boundary. A port extension: Raptor 7 has no such feature, but the saved .rbd opens in it.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor extract\fR [\-h] \-\-hierarchy NAME|ID [\-o FILE] [\-\-report\-hazards] [\-f {text,json}] [\-\-deps {up,system,refuse}] [\-\-pools {full,share,refuse}] [\-\-streams {keep,separate}] [\-\-treat KEY=VALUE] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build a standalone model from one hierarchy (its In node becomes Start, its Out node End) and save it, or list what crosses its boundary. A port extension: Raptor 7 has no such feature, but the saved .rbd opens in it.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-hierarchy\fR \fINAME|ID\fR

.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
write the extract here (.rbd or .rbds)
.TP
\fB\-\-report\-hazards\fR
list what crosses the boundary and the treatment each would get; write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR

.SS Isolated hierarchy (a port extension, not a raptor feature)
.TP
\fB\-\-deps\fR \fI{up|system|refuse}\fR
elements following something outside: assume it is always up (default), follow the extract's own end, or stop
.TP
\fB\-\-pools\fR \fI{full|share|refuse}\fR
spare and resource pools shared with outside blocks: the whole pool (default), scaled by the share of users inside, or stop
.TP
\fB\-\-streams\fR \fI{keep|separate}\fR
draws on a shared random stream: keep (default) or give each its own unused stream
.TP
\fB\-\-treat\fR \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
one item: block:ID.dep=up|system|refuse, pool:NAME.stock=N, resource:NAME.units=N; repeatable
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
List what crosses the Cooling hierarchy's boundary and what would be done about it.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor extract plant.rbd \-\-hierarchy Cooling \-\-report\-hazards\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Save Cooling as a standalone model that opens in Raptor 7.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor extract plant.rbd \-\-hierarchy Cooling \-o cooling.rbd \-\-deps system \-\-pools share\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
